nstructions. Add an explicit SHACL type/range constraint for each effectiveIceLoadCycleCount value, requiring it to be a QUDT QuantityValue (for example sh:class qudt:QuantityValue), in addition to the existing exact-one decimal constraint on qudt:numericValue and unit constraint. The current shape constrains only nested numericValue/unit paths and does not reject an effective result node of the wrong type."],"current_feedback":"Preserve the prior applicability and ship-owner instructions, but remove the unconditional sh:minCount 1/sh:maxCount 1 constraint on nltl:effectiveIceLoadCycleCount. The derived result is required only for a ship linked through nltl:hasComponent to an applicable nltl:propellerIceInteractionComponent; a ship with no such component must not fail merely because the result is absent. Encode conditional result existence and the bounded Nice*Z tolerance check without allowing missing applicability evidence or a missing required result on an applicable ship to pass. Retain the existing ship-owned operand paths, QUDT QuantityValue/type, decimal numericValue, unitless unit, and permitted arithmetic tolerance.","blocking":false,"semantic_attempt_consumed":false}
